<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">jewelcrafting</ansi> (skill)

Jewelcrafting is the art of shaping precious metals and gems into refined
adornments — rings, pendants, amulets, and bracelets. These pieces provide
subtle grace and enhancement to those who wear them. The skill is governed by
<ansi fg="yellow">Dexterity</ansi>, since fine work demands a steady hand.

Chrysalis settings are the bridge between jewelcrafting and enchanting. An
artificer uses these settings as vessels for living mutations, binding them
into items through long use.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   A <ansi fg="yellow">jeweler_bench</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             The Jeweler's Workshop is south of Town Square in Startland.
  Materials: Copper wire, silver wire, gold wire, gems, and gem dust.
             Find them on the ground in the Workshop or loot from foraging.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Known Recipes ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Copper Ring</ansi>           Skill 0   1x copper-wire, 1x gem-dust                2 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Simple Pendant</ansi>        Skill 3   1x copper-wire, 1x polished-stone           3 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Polished Stone Amulet</ansi>  Skill 8   2x polished-stone, 1x copper-wire           3 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Silver Ring</ansi>           Skill 12  1x silver-wire, 1x gem-dust                  3 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Chrysalis Setting</ansi>     Skill 15  1x copper-wire, 1x chrysalis-shard           4 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Gem-Set Necklace</ansi>      Skill 18  2x silver-wire, 1x raw-gem                   4 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Engraved Bracelet</ansi>     Skill 22  1x silver-wire, 2x gem-dust                  4 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Gold Signet Ring</ansi>      Skill 28  1x gold-wire, 1x gem-dust                   5 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Masterwork Gem Pendant</ansi> Skill 35  2x gold-wire, 2x raw-gem                    6 rounds

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Jewelcrafting improves through use. Each completed craft attempt (success or
failure) has a chance to advance the skill. Jewelcrafting progresses faster per
use than combat skills because crafting opportunities are less frequent.

There is no trainer for jewelcrafting — practice is the only teacher.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including jewelcrafting ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin crafting a jewelcrafting recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current jewelcrafting skill level.

